  "steps": [
    "Create an empty private kit directory at a caller-selected path.",
    "Acquire the pinned solc and Foundry forge images as described by the direct_downloads and archives records; check archive and executable SHA256 independently.",
    "For each sources row, fetch exactly the immutable source URL (or git show REVISION:source_path from the verified source checkout), verify byte count and SHA256, and write the unchanged bytes at kit_path. Preserve repository LICENSE notices alongside the source kit.",
    "Do not edit imported Solidity. The owned harness is separately pinned and imports the unchanged upstream properties and token models.",
    "Run superhunter.product_contract_properties_native.run(pathlib.Path(KIT)). The adapter builds in a fresh directory with offline Foundry, solc and a network namespace, executing only OwnedPropertiesReplayTest."
